            <ArticleTitle>Herniography in the investigation of groin pain in adults.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>805-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Herniography is a useful investigation in adults with unexplained groin pain in whom there is no clinical evidence of a hernia, thus ensuring appropriate surgery. The technique is described, normal anatomy and different types of hernias illustrated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
